ests you  the most and when you go through it  depending on what projects you are  working on what people your amazing it  will open another set of doors that you  know I like to multiply my doors I like  to make sure that once I will cram  through a door I have more doors opening  to me off to that so it's all about this  it's all about building your skills and  creating more opportunities for you okay  cool so now that you are a capital a  adult now I think it's really important  for you to take the time to get to know  yourself you've probably learned a lot  about yourself through high school in  college but you also have this  completely new part of your life that  you're embarking on and the person who's  going to lead that journey is you no one  else so I think it's always important to  ask yourself who you are what your  values are and what's important to you  especially at this time in your life and  like one great way of doing this is  honestly to try a bunch of stuff be  open-minded take every opportunity you  have because sure some of those things  you're gonna fail and some of those  things aren't going to work out but at  the end of the day you're going to learn  something about yourself or learn about  the world and I think that's a net  positive so I'm gonna continue mascha  store analogy so pretend that now you  have all these doors open but you have  to figure out which one is the best door  to choose and I think knowing yourself  and what's important to you and what  your values are is going to help you  make the right decisions choose the  right door and I know that sometimes  this can be really scary because it can  mean confronting your fears your doing  something that you're not super  comfortable with and one of the things  that I learned in the last couple of  years is to really learn how to embrace  that fear because doing so is going to  help you push a little bit out of your  comfort zone each time so that you're  always stretching yoursel